oad-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">DISPOSITIF DE DECOMPOSITION DE COMPOSES HALOGENES ORGANIQUES ET PROCEDE DE GESTION DE FONCTIONNEMENT AFFERENT, ET PROCEDE DE DECOMPOSITION DE COMPOSES HALOGENES ORGANIQUES</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-3222298-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>3222298</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-37010879-Y1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>37010879</doc-number><kind>Y1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7080287-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7080287</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-8323133-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8323133</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="US-5028452-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country> <doc-number>5028452</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5569810-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5569810</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>BESSHO MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATTORI TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI HEAVY IND LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BESSHO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATTORI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI HEAVY INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>BESSHO MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATTORI TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BESSHO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATTORI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic halogen compound decomposing device using plasma and capable of a positive and stable ignition at operation start-up and a stable post-ignition operation with a satisfactory plasma shape maintained, the device comprising a cylindrical waveguide (7) consisting of an outer conductor (8) and an inner conductor (9), and a dual-structure discharge pipe (5) installed coaxially with and inside the waveguide (7) and consisting of an inner pipe (11) and outer pipe (12). A probe antenna (9a) formed by extending the inner conductor (9) is disposed to surround the discharge pipe (5), and the tip end of the inner pipe (11) is positioned on the inner side of the tip end of the probe antenna (9a).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de décomposition de composés halogénés organiques utilisant du plasma et capable d'un allumage positif et stable lors du démarrage du fonctionnement et d'un fonctionnement post-allumage stable avec une forme de plasma satisfaisante maintenue, le dispositif comprenant un guide d'ondes cylindrique (7) constitué d'un conducteur extérieur (8) et d'un conducteur intérieur (9), ainsi qu'un conduit de décharge (5) à double structure disposé coaxialement par rapport au guide d'ondes (7) et à l'intérieur de celui-ci, et constitué d'un tube intérieur (11) et d'un tube extérieur (12). Une antenne à sonde (9a) formée par extension du conducteur intérieur (9) est disposée pour entourer le tube de décharge (5), et la pointe du tube intérieur (11) est positionnée sur le côté intérieur de la pointe de l'antenne à sonde (9a).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>